			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>OnlineID</FieldName>
			<FieldValue></FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Emulated Daemon</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Enable to have TP emulate amdaemon, in that case only the game .exe is needed</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Use Keyboard/Button For Axis</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>DirectInput only. Bind the separate stick directions in Controller Setup to use keyboard keys or controller buttons.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Keyboard/Button Axis X/Y Sensitivity</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>40</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Slider</FieldType>
			<FieldMin>1</FieldMin>
			<FieldMax>127</FieldMax>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Terminal Mode</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Start the game as the shop's terminal instead of a player's cabinet: a menu for watching recorded battles and battles that are going on, and for the rankings, with a card or as a guest. Nothing can be played there. Left stick (or the direction keys) to move, A to choose, B to go back.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>English Translation</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Enables english translation. TP includes a few small translations by default, but can load custom string translations from a translations.tsv next to the exe. </Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Graphics</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Resolution</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1920x1080</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>1280x720</string>
				<string>1600x900</string>
				<string>1920x1080</string>
				<string>2560x1440</string>
				<string>3200x1800</string>
				<string>3840x2160</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>The size the game renders at. Menus and text are laid out for 1920x1080 and scaled to it, so every size here keeps them as they are. In fullscreen the monitor must offer that mode (or the GPU's scaling, such as DSR or VSR, must): the game switches the display to it. In a window any size works.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Graphics</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Render Scale</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>100</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Slider</FieldType>
			<FieldMin>25</FieldMin>
			<FieldMax>100</FieldMax>
			<Hint>Renders the 3D picture at this percentage of the resolution's width and height and magnifies it to full size; menus and text stay at the full resolution. 100 renders everything at full size. Lower it if the game runs slowly: at 1920x1080, 67 renders the 3D picture at about 1280x720 and 50 at 960x540. On an integrated GPU 67 almost doubles the frame rate and 50 more than doubles it.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Graphics</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Upscaler</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>FSR</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>FSR</string>
				<string>Bilinear</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>How the 3D picture is magnified when Render Scale is below 100. FSR: AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0, close to the full resolution's sharpness, at a small cost (about 1.5 ms per frame on an integrated GPU). Bilinear: the game's own magnification, slightly faster but blurry.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Graphics</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>FSR Sharpness</FieldName>
			<VisibleWhen>Upscaler</VisibleWhen>
			<VisibleWhenValue>FSR</VisibleWhenValue>
			<FieldValue>0.2</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>0</string>
				<string>0.2</string>
				<string>0.5</string>
				<string>1</string>
				<string>2</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>How much FSR sharpens the magnified picture: 0 sharpens the most, and each step of 1 halves the sharpening. 0.2 is AMD's default; raise it if edges look grainy or jagged.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Online Battles</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Battles with other players. The battle runs on the PC of one of the players. Off: every battle is played alone with CPU controlled team mates and enemies.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Game Server Port</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>50100</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
			<Hint>Other players join battles hosted on this PC on this port (TCP and UDP) and the next one (UDP). Forward both in your router and allow the game in the firewall for the best connection; without that other players reach you through the server's relay.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Dedicated Host</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>For a PC that is left running in attract mode: other players' battles are started here before anywhere else.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Record Battles</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Battles that run on this PC are sent to the server while they are played, so that others can watch them, live or later. Needs about 30 KB/s of upload during a battle.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Battles In Attract Mode</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>While nobody plays, show battles of other players between the movies: one that is going on, and a recorded one.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>Online</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Rankings In Attract Mode</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>While nobody plays, show the rankings between the movies: the best players, and the battle points of the month.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
	</ConfigValues>
